+/* ---------------- Card Deck & Deal Patterns ---------------- */
+/* ============================================================
+   CANONICAL CARD MODEL
+   ------------------------------------------------------------
+   A card is exactly: { rank, suit }
+
+     rank: '2'..'9' | 'T' | 'J' | 'Q' | 'K' | 'A'   (T = ten)
+     suit: 'S' | 'H' | 'D' | 'C'                     (uppercase)
+
+   This is the SAME model used by cards-eval.js, so cards dealt here
+   can be handed straight to the evaluator with no translation.
+
+   Card IDENTITY (rank/suit) is immutable once dealt. Anything about
+   how a card is currently *shown* — face up/down, which seat holds it,
+   its position on the board — is render state and lives in the DOM or
+   in the table-state variables, never on the card object itself.
+
+   Presentation (suit symbol, red/black) is DERIVED from suit below,
+   never stored on the card.
+   ============================================================ */
+/* The canonical card model now lives in card-model.js — one authoritative
+   copy, shared by the app and the test suite. freshDeck is bound with `let`
+   because the deterministic tests substitute a stacked deck for it; the rest
+   are constants. */
